<div class="bg-white min-h-screen pt-16">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-gray mx-auto">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-5xl">
        Adaptics
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xl leading-8 text-gray-700 italic">
        In a world awash with information, the challenge is no longer access — it's adaptation.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
        Adaptics is a workshop for the mind. A collection of interactive experiments
        designed to help you see, shape, and navigate the invisible structures that
        govern how we understand complex systems.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
        Here you'll find tools for mapping what cannot be mapped geographically:
        relationships between ideas, flows of value, networks of influence. Each
        experiment is a lens—a different way of rendering the abstract into something
        you can rotate, probe, and play with.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
        This is not a finished product. It's a sketchbook and a place where
        half-formed intuitions about information environments take shape as interactive
        canvases, 3D visualizations, and dynamic simulations.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
        To adapt, you must first see clearly, with others. And to see clearly
        in an information environment, you need new instruments.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
        <p class="text-base text-gray-500">
          Get in touch:
          <a
            href="https://x.com/randw"
            class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500 ml-1">
            @randw
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-500 mt-2">
          View the source:
          <a
            href="https://github.com/afomi/adaptics"
            class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-500 ml-1">
            github.com/afomi/adaptics
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
